Chapter 8: Thermodynamic Feasibility and Conservation

8.1 Entropy and Exergy Constraints

The second law S_{\text{gen},i}\ge 0 forbids certain transformations, even if the AI finds them "optimal." Exergy destruction X_{\text{dest},i}\ge 0 is proportional to entropy production.

8.2 Physical Admissibility

The physical admissibility set:

\mathcal{K}_{\text{physics}}=\left\{z\in\mathcal{Z}\;\middle|\;\exists u:\text{ balances hold and }S_{\text{gen},i}\ge0,\;X_{\text{dest},i}\ge0\right\}

is a structural constraint on feasible dynamics. It is not policy-dependent.

8.3 The Conservation Theorem

Theorem 2. No policy can achieve autonomy on \mathcal{K} if \mathcal{K}_{\text{physics}}\cap\operatorname{Viab}_\beta(\mathcal{K})=\emptyset.

Proof sketch. If thermodynamic constraints are infeasible on the viability kernel, then no admissible trajectory can remain in \mathcal{K} indefinitely. The viability probability V^*(z_0) is zero for all z_0 in the intersection. Therefore, no policy can achieve autonomy. \square

8.4 Discrete Manufacturing

For discrete manufacturing (assembly, not thermal process), Shannon entropy of queues as proxy for disorder is an open modeling question. We restrict thermodynamic analysis to process nodes where thermal constraints are physically meaningful.

---

Chapter 9: Reconfiguration Theory

9.1 Structural Conditions

The reconfiguration operator \Gamma must satisfy structural conditions, not merely preserve properties. The graph operation v_k\notin V_{t+1} plus edge rewiring must preserve connectivity of material flow graph and preserve rank of observability Gramian \lambda_{\min}(W_o)\ge\epsilon.

9.2 Koren RMS Principles as Algebraic Conditions

The six Koren RMS principles translate to algebraic conditions on \Gamma:

· Modularity: \Gamma decomposes into independent sub-operations.
· Integrability: \Gamma preserves interface compatibility.
· Diagnosability: \Gamma preserves failure detection capability.
· Convertibility: \Gamma preserves mode reachability.
· Customization: \Gamma preserves quality constraints.
· Scalability: \Gamma preserves observability rank.

9.3 The Reconfiguration Theorem

Theorem 3. If \Gamma\in\mathcal{G}_{\text{adm}}, then \Gamma preserves the Black Factory property under A1–A7.

Proof sketch. Conditions (i)–(iv) of A6 ensure that \Gamma preserves viability, observability, thermodynamic feasibility, and safety. Therefore, the four conditions of Theorem 1 remain satisfied. \square

