Chapter 10: Decidability Boundaries and Complexity

10.1 POMDP Complexity

· Finite-horizon POMDP: Computing an optimal policy is PSPACE-complete (Papadimitriou & Tsitsiklis, 1987).
· Infinite-horizon POMDP: Optimal policy existence is undecidable (Madani, Hanks & Condon, 2003).

The hybrid POMDP is at least as hard as the discrete POMDP.

10.2 Hybrid Observability Undecidability

Observability of piecewise-affine hybrid systems is undecidable because many classes simulate Turing machines (Collins & van Schuppen, 2004).

10.3 Petri Net State Explosion

Reachability graph size grows exponentially with nodes/marking. Hierarchical decomposition mitigates explosion without altering theoretical foundation. The literature addresses "the well-known combinatorial explosion issue" in Timed Petri Nets.

10.4 Decidable Regimes

For piecewise-affine systems with no Turing machine simulation, observability is decidable. Under A7, necessity direction of Theorem 1 is attainable.

