Chapter 11: Industrial Validation and Sim-to-Real Roadmap

11.1 Industrial Evidence

Siemens Amberg. 75% of value chain automated; 99.9988% quality; ~12 defects per million.

FANUC. 50 clones/day; autonomous operation up to a month.

Foxconn. >95% automation; 190% labor productivity; 99.5% OTD; 45% cost cut.

These cases confirm lights-out manufacturing is not merely futuristic vision. But they remain partially open-loop at model adaptation and structural reconfiguration levels.

11.2 The Sim-to-Real Gap

"The sim-to-real transfer gap continue[s] to hinder the widespread industrial application of RL." RL "is still limited to industrial applications and suffers from three major challenges: sample inefficiency, real data collection, and the gap between simulator and reality."

11.3 Validation Roadmap

We propose:

1. Digital Model Playground: Coating scenario simulation.
2. Hardware-in-the-loop: Physical integration testing.
3. Continuous operation testing: 1000-hour continuous operation for sim-to-real quantification.

No specific standard for 1000-hour autonomous operation was found in the literature. This remains a proposed validation protocol.

