Appendix E: Autonomy Metrics and Aggregation

E.1 Vector-Valued Autonomy Profile

\mathbf{A}_{\mathrm{BF}}=(A_I,A_D,A_P,A_M,R_F)

Informational Autonomy A_I:

A_I = 1 - \frac{H(b_t)}{H_{\max}}

where H(b_t) is the entropy of the belief state and H_{\max} is the maximum entropy over the state space. Alternatively, A_I can be defined via the normalized observability Gramian eigenvalue:

A_I = \frac{\lambda_{\min}(W_o)}{\lambda_{\max}(W_o)}

Decisional Autonomy A_D:

A_D = 1 - \frac{J(\pi^*)-J(\pi)}{J(\pi^*)}

where J(\pi) is the expected return of the learned policy and J(\pi^*) is the oracle optimum in a known environment.

Physical Autonomy A_P: Degree of actuation and reconfiguration capability without human intervention. Defined as the fraction of actions in \mathcal{U}(z_t) that are executable without human authorization.

Maintenance Autonomy A_M: Ability to predict, diagnose, and repair failures autonomously. Defined as the fraction of failure modes detectable and repairable without human intervention.

Resilience R_F: Ratio of post-disturbance performance to nominal performance, extended to reconfiguration speed. The POC (Penalty of Change) metric is "the most practically valuable quantitative resilience metric to assess the level of resilience in human-centered CPPS workstations in SMEs":

\mathrm{POC} = \sum_{i=1}^{D} P n(X_i) P r(X_i)

where D is the number of potential changes, P n(X_i) is the penalty associated with change X_i, and P r(X_i) is the probability of change X_i.

E.2 Aggregation via Liebig's Law

A_{\mathrm{BF}} = \min_i A_i

Justification: Autonomy fails if any loop fails. A system with perfect informational autonomy but zero maintenance autonomy is not a Black Factory. The minimum captures the bottleneck property of autonomy.

E.3 Alternative Aggregation: Viability Margin

A_{\mathrm{BF}} = d(z,\partial\mathcal{K})

where d(z,\partial\mathcal{K}) is the distance from the current state z to the boundary of the safe set \mathcal{K}. This measures the safety margin of the system.

